=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play updates/dormant-jobs ------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: updates/dormant-jobs$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.23 (OpenRC). alpine323 with$
# logrotate's daily job, crond stopped. Enable starts crond and$
# says it starts logrotate too; Disable stops it again.$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured no apk-cron$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] apk-cron             Not installed$
  [ ] crond                Stopped not at boot$
   -  Other Jobs           logrotate use crond$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable automatic updates$
      Daily, by apk-cron$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Enable automatic updates #####################################$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  Auto Updates         On$
   -  Also starts          logrotate$
$
   -  Turn on daily upgrades$
      crond$
      -apk-cron not installed, crond stopped$
      +apk-cron installed, crond started at boot$
      $ apk add apk-cron$
      $ rc-update add crond default$
      $ rc-service crond start$
$
   -  Record hardn's changes$
      /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json$
$
  Turn automatic updates on? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Turn on daily upgrades  Done$
  [+] Record hardn's changes  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured apk-cron$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  apk-cron             Installed$
   -  Daily Script         In place /etc/periodic/daily/apk$
   -  crond                Running starts at boot$
   -  Other Jobs           logrotate use crond$
   -  Turned on by         hardn record of 2026-10-20$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable automatic updates$
      Undo hardn's changes$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Disable automatic updates ####################################$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  Auto Updates         Off$
   -  Rollback             Reinstalls from the repositories$
$
   -  Stop crond$
      crond$
      $ rc-service crond stop$
$
   -  Stop crond at boot$
      crond$
      $ rc-update del crond default$
$
   -  Remove apk-cron$
      apk-cron$
      $ apk del apk-cron$
$
   -  Delete hardn's record$
      /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json$
$
  Turn automatic updates off? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Stop crond             Done$
  [+] Stop crond at boot     Done$
  [+] Remove apk-cron        Done$
  [+] Delete hardn's record  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
